For #2476: When encountering the `-10005: noWindowsAvailable` error in native macOS UI automation, you can handle this by implementing a retry mechanism. Before attempting to interact with the UI element, check if the accessibility object for the element still exists. If not, wait for a short period and retry. This can be implemented as a PR in the `your-repo/actions` file:

```diff
- const interactWithElement = async (element) => {
+ const interactWithElement = async (element) => {
+     const retryCount = 3;
+     for (let i = 0; i < retryCount; i++) {
+         if (element) {
+             await performActions(element);
+             break;
+         } else if (i === retryCount - 1) {
+             console.error(`No element found after ${retryCount} attempts. Skipping interaction.`);
+             return;
+         } else {
+             await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 500));
+         }
+     }
+     await interactWithElement(element); // Retrying the interaction
+ }
```

